Create an API key

Usage:
  flint api-keys create [flags]

Arguments and flags:
  --access full|read_only|restricted     Key access. Full and read_only resolve from the current scope catalog for the key's mode; restricted holds only its listed scopes. Granting full or read_only requires a freshly verified authorized user session or a full-access API key. (required; --scopes alone selects restricted)
  --expires-at TIME                      RFC3339 timestamp. Accepts RFC3339, calendar dates in the reporting timezone, now, +30d or -2h; relative body times require a sign.
  --name TEXT                            Set name. (required)
  --partner-app-install-id pinst_ID      Links this key to a connected app's install. Revoking the install or its grant for this key's environment revokes the key. The install must be active and authorized for that environment. Set only at creation; it never changes. Omit for an unlinked key. Keys created by a linked key inherit its link. Each install can have up to 25 linked keys that have not been revoked per environment.
    Accepts @last.pinst for the most recent resource this profile created or changed.
  --scopes TEXT[,TEXT...]                The scopes to grant. Required only with access restricted; forbidden with full or read_only. (required for --access restricted)
    96 values: flint schema command api-keys.create --output json
    Repeat this flag for multiple values.
  --input TEXT                           JSON body: FILE.json, - for stdin, or inline JSON

Request body:
  Required top-level fields: access, name
  Run flint schema input api-keys.create --output json for the full schema.
  --input takes FILE.json, - for stdin, or inline JSON.

Global flags:
  --context ID  Select an authorized context for this command
  --output human|json|ndjson  --quiet  --debug  --no-input  --live  --merchant ID  --profile NAME
  --credential-store keyring|file  Credential backend (or FLINT_CREDENTIAL_STORE; defaults to the profile store or keyring)

Capability flags:
  --idempotency-key KEY  --dry-run=client  --confirm  --field PATH (inside the resource; strings raw, other values JSON)  --select FIELDS (inside each resource)  --jq EXPR  --timeout DURATION
  --timeout is the total request budget including retries (default 150s).

Examples:
  flint api-keys create --access=restricted --expires-at='2027-03-17T14:30:00Z' --name='Sandbox orders integration' --scopes=accounts.api_keys.read --scopes=commerce.orders.read --scopes=commerce.orders.write
